# Flutter Feature Flags

Feature flags are managed through the `JumpFeatureManager` and its change provider. The service listens to live changes and then using `getValue` on that riverpod provider we can get live rebuilds with flags.

Flags are used to control any moderately sized new piece of functionality or large scale refactors

## Where Flags are

- Flags are defined either globally in `features.dart` or locally in `*_features.dart` where `*` is the app name, i.e. Kiosk

## Creating Flags

Flags are created using the `create-feature-flag` skill. This creates them locally and remotely
